Saily: licence

The Saily software is released under the MIT License, reproduced below.

The data bundled with the software is NOT covered by the MIT License. Each data
file keeps the terms of its source; the full list is in NOTICE and the
explanation in docs/LICENSING.md. In short:

- site/passages/<id>/chart-data.js, and every file that embeds it (dist/saily.html,
  tools/out/saily-standalone.html): a Derivative Database of OpenStreetMap
  data, (c) OpenStreetMap contributors, Open Database License (ODbL) 1.0.
  Attribution and share-alike apply. It may only be redistributed under ODbL.
- Traffic separation scheme positions from IMO COLREG.2/Circ.66 (in
  passages/strait-of-gibraltar.tss.json and site/passages/<id>/chart-data.js): reproduced as
  facts. The circular itself is (c) International Maritime Organization and is
  not reproduced.
- Pilotage notes quoting NGA Pub 131, Sailing Directions (Enroute) Western
  Mediterranean (in passages/*.json and site/passages/<id>/passage.js): a work of the
  United States Government, public domain.
- tools/fixtures/fc.json, tools/fixtures/marine.json, tools/out/wx_snapshot.json
  and the forecast embedded in dist/saily.html: weather data by
  Open-Meteo.com, Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International (CC BY 4.0).
- site/vendor/leaflet/: Leaflet 1.9.4, BSD-2-Clause, see
  site/vendor/leaflet/LICENSE.
- Map tiles and depth data from OpenStreetMap, OpenSeaMap, Esri and
  EMODnet are fetched at run time under the providers' own terms and are not
  part of this repository.

Nothing in this repository is an official nautical chart or a substitute for
one. Use official charts, keep a lookout and obey the COLREGs.

